---@field Heading? aws.geo_routes.Heading|distilled.Secret The initial direction of travel in degrees (0-360, where 0 is north). This can affect which road segments are considered accessible from the starting point.
---@field Matching? aws.geo_routes.IsolineMatchingOptions Controls how the destination point is matched to the road network, including search radius and name-based matching preferences.
---@field SideOfStreet? aws.geo_routes.IsolineSideOfStreetOptions Specifies which side of the street should be considered accessible, which is important when building entrances or parking access points are only reachable from one side of the road.

