---A leg is a section of a route from one waypoint to the next. A leg could be of type Vehicle, Pedestrian or Ferry. Legs of different types could occur together within a single route. For example, a car employing the use of a Ferry will contain Vehicle legs corresponding to journey on land, and Ferry legs corresponding to the journey via Ferry.
---@class aws.geo_routes.RouteLeg
---@field FerryLegDetails? aws.geo_routes.RouteFerryLegDetails FerryLegDetails is populated when the Leg type is Ferry, and provides additional information that is specific to ferry travel. Not supported in ap-southeast-1 and ap-southeast-5 regions for GrabMaps customers.
---@field Geometry aws.geo_routes.RouteLegGeometry Geometry of the area to be avoided.
---@field Language? aws.geo_routes.LanguageTag List of languages for instructions within steps in the response. Not supported in ap-southeast-1 and ap-southeast-5 regions for GrabMaps customers.
---@field PedestrianLegDetails? aws.geo_routes.RoutePedestrianLegDetails Details related to the pedestrian leg.
---@field TravelMode distilled.Secret Specifies the mode of transport when calculating a route. Used in estimating the speed of travel and road compatibility.
---@field Type distilled.Secret Type of the leg.
---@field VehicleLegDetails? aws.geo_routes.RouteVehicleLegDetails Details related to the vehicle leg.
---@field RentalLegDetails? aws.geo_routes.RouteRentalLegDetails Details related to the rental leg.
---@field TaxiLegDetails? aws.geo_routes.RouteTaxiLegDetails Details related to the taxi leg.
---@field TransitLegDetails? aws.geo_routes.RouteTransitLegDetails Details related to the transit leg.

---@alias aws.geo_routes.RouteLegAdditionalFeature "Elevation"|"Incidents"|"PassThroughWaypoints"|"Summary"|"Tolls"|"TravelStepInstructions"|"TruckRoadTypes"|"TypicalDuration"|"Zones"|"Bookings"|"IntermediateStops"|"NextDepartures"

---@alias aws.geo_routes.RouteLegAdditionalFeatureList (aws.geo_routes.RouteLegAdditionalFeature|string)[]

