---@field RouteNumber? aws.geo_routes.RouteNumber Route number of the road.

---@alias aws.geo_routes.RouteMajorRoadLabelList aws.geo_routes.RouteMajorRoadLabel[]

---Options related to route matching.
---@class aws.geo_routes.RouteMatchingOptions
---@field NameHint? aws.geo_routes.SensitiveString|distilled.Secret Attempts to match the provided position to a road similar to the provided name.
---@field OnRoadThreshold? aws.geo_routes.DistanceMeters|distilled.Secret If the distance to a highway/bridge/tunnel/sliproad is within threshold, the waypoint will be snapped to the highway/bridge/tunnel/sliproad.
---@field Radius? aws.geo_routes.DistanceMeters|distilled.Secret Considers all roads within the provided radius to match the provided destination to. The roads that are considered are determined by the provided Strategy.
---@field Strategy? aws.geo_routes.MatchingStrategy|string Strategy that defines matching of the position onto the road network. MatchAny considers all roads possible, whereas MatchMostSignificantRoad matches to the most significant road.

---@alias aws.geo_routes.RouteMatrix aws.geo_routes.RouteMatrixRow[]

---Allow Options related to the route matrix.
---@class aws.geo_routes.RouteMatrixAllowOptions
---@field Hot? aws.geo_routes.SensitiveBoolean|distilled.Secret Allow Hot (High Occupancy Toll) lanes while calculating the route.
---@field Hov? aws.geo_routes.SensitiveBoolean|distilled.Secret Allow Hov (High Occupancy vehicle) lanes while calculating the route.

---AutoCircle requests the route matrix service to define a Circle boundary that best attempts to include most waypoints (Origins and Destinations) using the AutoCircle settings. Any waypoints outside of the auto-defined Circle boundary will be considered out of the routing boundary, which results in a route matrix entry error.
---@class aws.geo_routes.RouteMatrixAutoCircle
---@field Margin? aws.geo_routes.DistanceMeters|distilled.Secret The minimal distance, in meters, between any waypoint and the perimeter of the circle auto-defined for the boundary. Some margin is usually recommended so that the routing has enough leeway to travel from one waypoint to another optimally without conflicting with the routing boundary.
---@field MaxRadius? aws.geo_routes.DistanceMeters|distilled.Secret The maximum radius, in meters, that the auto-defined Circle boundary should have, before the Margin distance is added to the circle.

---Area to be avoided.
---@class aws.geo_routes.RouteMatrixAvoidanceArea
---@field Geometry aws.geo_routes.RouteMatrixAvoidanceAreaGeometry Geometry of the area to be avoided.

---Geometry of the area to be avoided.
---@class aws.geo_routes.RouteMatrixAvoidanceAreaGeometry
---@field BoundingBox? aws.geo_routes.BoundingBox|distilled.Secret Geometry defined as a bounding box. The first pair represents the X and Y coordinates (longitude and latitude,) of the southwest corner of the bounding box; the second pair represents the X and Y coordinates (longitude and latitude) of the northeast corner.
---@field Polygon? aws.geo_routes.LinearRings Geometry defined as a polygon with only one linear ring.
---@field PolylinePolygon? aws.geo_routes.PolylineRingList A list of Isoline PolylinePolygon, for each isoline PolylinePolygon, it contains PolylinePolygon of the first linear ring (the outer ring) and from second item to the last item (the inner rings). For more information on polyline encoding, see https://github.com/aws-geospatial/polyline.

---@alias aws.geo_routes.RouteMatrixAvoidanceAreaList aws.geo_routes.RouteMatrixAvoidanceArea[]

---Specifies options for areas to avoid when calculating the route. This is a best-effort avoidance setting, meaning the router will try to honor the avoidance preferences but may still include restricted areas if no feasible alternative route exists. If avoidance options are not followed, the response will indicate that the avoidance criteria were violated.
---@class aws.geo_routes.RouteMatrixAvoidanceOptions
---@field Areas? aws.geo_routes.RouteMatrixAvoidanceAreaList Areas to be avoided.
---@field CarShuttleTrains? aws.geo_routes.SensitiveBoolean|distilled.Secret Avoid car-shuttle-trains while calculating the route.
---@field ControlledAccessHighways? aws.geo_routes.SensitiveBoolean|distilled.Secret Avoid controlled access highways while calculating the route.
---@field DirtRoads? aws.geo_routes.SensitiveBoolean|distilled.Secret Avoid dirt roads while calculating the route.
---@field Ferries? aws.geo_routes.SensitiveBoolean|distilled.Secret Avoid ferries while calculating the route.
---@field TollRoads? aws.geo_routes.SensitiveBoolean|distilled.Secret Avoids roads where the specified toll transponders are the only mode of payment.
---@field TollTransponders? aws.geo_routes.SensitiveBoolean|distilled.Secret Avoids roads where the specified toll transponders are the only mode of payment.
---@field TruckRoadTypes? aws.geo_routes.TruckRoadTypeList Truck road type identifiers. BK1 through BK4 apply only to Sweden. A2,A4,B2,B4,C,D,ET2,ET4 apply only to Mexico.
---@field Tunnels? aws.geo_routes.SensitiveBoolean|distilled.Secret Avoid tunnels while calculating the route.
---@field UTurns? aws.geo_routes.SensitiveBoolean|distilled.Secret Avoid U-turns for calculation on highways and motorways.
---@field ZoneCategories? aws.geo_routes.RouteMatrixAvoidanceZoneCategoryList Zone categories to be avoided.

---Zone categories to be avoided.
---@class aws.geo_routes.RouteMatrixAvoidanceZoneCategory
---@field Category? aws.geo_routes.RouteMatrixZoneCategory|string|distilled.Secret Zone category to be avoided.

---@alias aws.geo_routes.RouteMatrixAvoidanceZoneCategoryList aws.geo_routes.RouteMatrixAvoidanceZoneCategory[]

---Boundary within which the matrix is to be calculated. All data, origins and destinations outside the boundary are considered invalid.
---@class aws.geo_routes.RouteMatrixBoundary
---@field Geometry? aws.geo_routes.RouteMatrixBoundaryGeometry Geometry of the area to be avoided.
---@field Unbounded? aws.geo_routes.SensitiveBoolean|distilled.Secret No restrictions in terms of a routing boundary, and is typically used for longer routes.

---Geometry of the routing boundary.
---@class aws.geo_routes.RouteMatrixBoundaryGeometry
---@field AutoCircle? aws.geo_routes.RouteMatrixAutoCircle AutoCircle requests the route matrix service to define a Circle boundary that best attempts to include most waypoints (Origins and Destinations) using the AutoCircle settings. Any waypoints outside of the auto-defined Circle boundary will be considered out of the routing boundary, which results in a route matrix entry error.
---@field Circle? aws.geo_routes.Circle|distilled.Secret Geometry defined as a circle. The circle defines the routing boundary area. Any waypoints outside the circle will result in a route matrix entry error.
---@field BoundingBox? aws.geo_routes.BoundingBox|distilled.Secret Geometry defined as a bounding box. The first pair represents the X and Y coordinates (longitude and latitude,) of the southwest corner of the bounding box; the second pair represents the X and Y coordinates (longitude and latitude) of the northeast corner.
---@field Polygon? aws.geo_routes.LinearRings Geometry defined as a polygon with only one linear ring. A linear ring is a closed sequence of four or more coordinates. The first and last coordinates are the same, forming a closed boundary. Each coordinate is a position in [longitude, latitude] format.

---Travel mode options when the provided travel mode is Car.
---@class aws.geo_routes.RouteMatrixCarOptions
---@field LicensePlate? aws.geo_routes.RouteMatrixVehicleLicensePlate|distilled.Secret The vehicle License Plate.
---@field MaxSpeed? aws.geo_routes.SpeedKilometersPerHour|distilled.Secret Maximum speed
---@field Occupancy? aws.geo_routes.SensitiveInteger|distilled.Secret The number of occupants in the vehicle.

---The route destination.
